Why vendored: the Jetson tracking-overlay publisher already runs MediaMTX
v1.20.0 and exposes the same stream over WHEP. Using the reader that ships
with that exact server version keeps the browser signalling path matched to
the deployed server instead of reimplementing WHEP.

Local modifications (all marked "NavPy patch" in reader.js):
  1. #releaseSession() -- single, idempotent DELETE of the WHEP session
     resource, using the URL captured from the POST Location header.
  2. close() -- releases that session, clears the restart timer, drops the
     peer connection and queued candidates, and is safe to call twice.
  3. #handleError() -- reuses #releaseSession() instead of its inline DELETE.
  4. #sendOffer() -- a 201 that arrives after close() releases the session the
     server just created, and stops the chain without arming a restart.
  5. ES module export added alongside the upstream window global.

